2026-01-30 17:11:05 | OUTPUT |     
2026-01-30 17:11:05 | OUTPUT |     Joke 2 is broader in its absurdity, imagining a "Ministry of Grumpy Faces" and bureaucratic nitpicking over travel itineraries. This is more relatable – everyone has experienced frustrating bureaucracy – and the image of a ministry dedicated to grumpiness is inherently funny. The "complete mess" paperwork adds to the comedic effect. It's a stronger connection to the idea of diplomatic tensions being fragile and easily disrupted. It also feels more natural in its delivery. While both jokes are relatively economical, Joke 2's phrasing is slightly tighter and more impactful.
2026-01-30 17:11:05 | OUTPUT |     
2026-01-30 17:11:05 | OUTPUT |     Joke 1's strength is its unexpectedness, but its weakness is its lack of logical grounding. Joke 2's strength is its relatable absurdity and stronger connection to the core issue of diplomatic protocol.
